WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.710
Your coding conversations keep growing.

2
00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:07.270
Useful decisions get buried, and switching computers can mean losing context.

3
00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:14.450
Mem Maestro brings project memory, session sync, and safe Claude archives into one plugin.

4
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.710
Start inside your project's Git repository.

5
00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:22.100
Run setup on each machine, then connect your own memory store.

6
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:27.010
Sessions can sync through Google Drive or a private GitHub repository.

7
00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.610
Choose private GitHub if you want Claude session archiving.

8
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.450
Already installed?

9
00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:37.450
Run update on every device before using this release's AI features.

10
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.790
Restart your agent, and approve updated hooks if it asks.

11
00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:49.470
Next, choose the coding client you already use: Codex, Claude Code, or Copilot.

12
00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.790
Enable semantic search and automatic summaries.

13
00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:58.980
Mem Maestro uses that client's existing sign-in, without requesting a separate API key.

14
00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.570
Model calls use your account's allowance.

15
00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:06.210
As you work, supported hooks capture small assistant observations.

16
00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.850
Original sessions stay separate.

17
00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:15.010
A background worker turns saved notes into concise summaries with source references.

18
00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:20.310
Those summaries are AI interpretations, so you can inspect the original notes.

19
00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:23.330
Ask a question in your own words.

20
00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:27.090
Hybrid search combines keywords with AI ranking.

21
00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:30.890
Open a returned memory ID to read the details.

22
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:36.050
Results show how much was searched; this does not scan every archived conversation.

23
00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:42.110
To reclaim native Claude storage, first measure usage and preview an archive.

24
00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:47.660
Close all Claude processes, then archive a selected inactive session.

25
00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:53.010
Local files are removed only after the cloud snapshot is downloaded and verified.

26
00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:57.110
Small graph nodes keep references to archived sessions.

27
00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:03.320
When older history is needed, recall downloads the selected archive, verifies it,

28
00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:07.110
reads the requested portion, and removes the temporary copy.

29
00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.670
Your useful knowledge stays searchable.

30
00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.830
Your history stays recoverable.

31
00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.370
Your storage stays under your control.
